fourth place."] "\n\n" [:p {} "Uetake retired from competition after the 1968 Olympics and became a coach at his alma mater, settling in Oklahoma. Behm won the 1970 Tbilisi International Tournament and the 1971 Pan American gold medal, but never made another Olympic team. Talebi’s bronze was a standard for him, as he had also placed third at the 1966-67 Worlds and would win another World Championship bronze in 1969."] "\n"] [:table {:class "table table-striped"} [:thead {} [:tr {} [:th {} "Pos"] [:th {} "Number"] [:th {} "Competitor"] [:th {} "NOC"] [:th {} "Round Eliminated"] [:th {} "Bad Points"] [:th {}] [:th {}] [:th {}]]] [:tbody {} [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "1"] [:td {:class "bib"} "8"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/59112"} "Yojiro Uetake"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/JPN"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/JPN.png"}] "JPN"]] [:td {} "–"] [:td {} "–"] [:td {} [:span {:class "Gold"} "Gold"]] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "2"] [:td {:class "bib"} "20"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/60573"} "Don Behm"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/USA"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/USA.png"}] "USA"]] [:td {} "–"] [:td {} "–"] [:td {} [:span {:class "Silver"} "Silver"]] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "3"] [:td {:class "bib"} "17"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/58768"} "Abutaleb Talebi"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/IRI"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/IRI.png"}] "IRI"]] [:td {} "–"] [:td {} "–"] [:td {} [:span {:class "Bronze"} "Bronze"]] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "4"] [:td {:class "bib"} "14"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/60442"} "Ali Aliyev"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/URS"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertic